{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["And the reason for <b>for the judgment is Elohim's</b> is like the reason of 'for you do not judge for man but for HaShem, and He is with you in the matter of judgment' (II Chronicles 19:6) — to say that it belongs to Elohim to execute judgment among His creatures, for therefore He created them, that there should be uprightness and righteousness among them, and to rescue the plundered from the hand of the oppressor — and He has appointed you in His place. And if you shrink back and commit violence, behold you have sinned against HaShem, for you have betrayed His commission."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:13:49.028891067Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}